      "type": "HostPhase",
      "group": "metal.pk.io",
      "source": "metal/api/v1alpha1/host_types.go",
      "description": "HostPhase summarizes a machine's conditions together with whether it is claimed. Enrolling and Inspecting mean the cluster is still finding out what the machine is; Available means it is understood and free; Assigned means something claimed it; Provisioning means work is happening to it right now and Provisioned that the work finished; Releasing means it is being handed back. Failed and Maintenance are the two stops: Failed when an install did not work, Maintenance while a person has set the metal.pk.io/maintenance annotation.\n\nAssigned and Provisioning are deliberately separate. A machine can be spoken for without anything disruptive happening to it, and conflating the two leaves no way to say so.",
